  "articleBody": "Adding an extra bathroom to a home provides essential everyday convenience and boosts resale value. However, creating a bathroom where none existed before requires substantial plumbing, electrical, and structural preparation.\n\nKey Benefits\nA dedicated guest bath, primary en suite, or basement bathroom eliminates morning bottlenecks and makes your home far more comfortable for family and visitors.\n\nProcess Breakdown\nThe job begins by mapping drainage routes, slope, and vent stacks. Once building and trade permits are secured, framing, rough plumbing, electrical wiring, and exhaust ventilation are installed. Rough inspections happen before backer boards, specialized waterproofing, tile, and fixtures go in.\n\nReal Examples\nWhether tying into a crawl space in Littleton or cutting into a concrete slab for drainage pipes in Aurora, proper drain slopes and reliable waterproofing membranes make the difference between lasting durability and leaks.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\nThe distance between your planned fixtures and the existing main sewer stack determines construction complexity. Placing a new bath directly above or adjacent to existing lines keeps costs significantly lower.\n\nConnect with Abraham at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to review your bathroom addition goals and review your layout options.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}